    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Continuous Renal Replacement Therapy (CRRT) is a 24-hour dialysis treatment used in critical care patients with renal failure who cannot tolerate three to four-hour intermittent dialysis sessions. The CRRT machine is an advanced technology operated only by trained critical care nurses, who must understand the principles on which the machine works, circuitry, modes, and troubleshooting. Knowledge and understanding is reinforced through practice and experience, resulting in a more efﬁcient and conﬁdent process.",
